# Blossom Assistant (extension)

Client for ChatRouter at `http://127.0.0.1:8081`. Local-first coding.

**Offline priority:** no internet escalation as the product path. See `.cursor/rules/offline-priority.mdc`. Hardware gaps are open problems — solve locally, do not route to cloud.

## Ownership (do not invert)

- **Extension:** editor attach, repo knowledge, disk checks (`fs.access`), Apply / auto-apply / auto-save, fence→file mapping, UI summary.
- **ChatRouter:** routing (persona/coder/cloud), RAG, coding_rules, GGUF hot-swap.
- ChatRouter cannot see the project disk unless the extension puts facts in the prompt. **Disk truth = extension.**

## Critical rules

- **CREATE vs EDIT:** new files get their own fence (`path=contacts.html`); never dump a new page into attached `index.html`.
- Multi-file = multiple path-labeled fences (or `**file.ext**` heading above fence). Apply must create all of them.
- Parse path from: `path=…`, bold/heading above fence, HTML comments — **never** invent paths from `<title>` (caused `validhtmlexample.html`).
- Auto-apply + auto-save must land on disk without Ctrl+S.
- **search_replace UX:** each replace shows a PR-style chat card (Removed/Added + file hunks) in realtime; optional side-by-side `vscode.diff` via `blossom.edits.openDiffOnReplace` (default on). Compare button reopens the diff after apply.
- **Content guard** (`editGuard.ts`): block full replaces that paste README/markdown into `.py`/code files, ### path headings, plan stubs, or gut source. Blocks empty/near-empty wipes, line-ratio gutting (even when scoreCode is weak — PHP used to cap at 1 and skip all oldCode≥3 checks), structure collapse, and markdown/stub patterns (e.g. darcutil-style). Docs go in `path=*.md` fences.
- **Dry-run gate** (`dryRunGate.ts`): block Apply/auto-apply on `patch_*.py`, `deploy_*.py`, `tools/*.py` until `python <path> --dry-run` (or smoke import) succeeds in the same turn. Toggle: `blossom.edits.dryRunGate`.
- **Patch script guard** (`patchScriptContext.ts`): auto-scans workspace for patch scripts; injects `[PATCH SCRIPT MAP]`; blocks cross-file symbols and oversized rewrites.
- **Ghidra read_ghidra** (`ghidra/client.ts`): HTTP client for any Ghidra MCP bridge; auto-discovers localhost ports; injects `[GHIDRA]` hint when connected. Tool: decompile/disassemble/function_info/search_functions.
- **Analysis-first routing**: prompts with "Before making any code modifications" / Problem Analysis + Litmus → plan-only until user says implement. Saves tokens on RE tasks.
- After coding: Summary card with model notes + backend (Local coder / Claude / Gemini). No "Done — applied…" spam.
- **Live UX:** agent tool loop uses `streamPlain` / `streamChat` only (never `chatOnce`) so reasoning + answer tokens stream live. `model_reasoning` shows in the busy-row reasoning strip; do not add a "Thinking · N steps" trail box.
- Link / unused-file asks:
  - Inject `[LINK CHECK]` with EXISTS/MISSING from real `fs.access`.
  - Never remove EXISTS links.
  - "Delete unused / safe to delete" = extension proposes `kind: delete` for `[UNUSED FILES]` and Apply/Auto-apply unlinks (model fences ignored in that mode).
  - Explicit deletes: resolve user name (e.g. `marks` → `marks.html`) against workspace disk; lock deletes to those targets so the model cannot delete a different file.
  - Explicit `DELETE path=file.ext` / ```delete path=…``` also become delete Apply cards when not locked out.
  - Inject clear `[TASK BRIEF]` so the model does not confuse orphans with dead links.

## Key files

- `src/agent/editorContext.ts` — LINK CHECK, UNUSED FILES, task brief
- `src/agent/applyFromResponse.ts` — fence→Apply
- `src/agent/editGuard.ts` — block prose-in-code / gutted full replaces
- `src/agent/dryRunGate.ts` — require --dry-run before patch-script apply
- `src/agent/patchScriptContext.ts` — patch file map + cross-file / cave guards
- `src/ghidra/client.ts` — read_ghidra HTTP bridge client
- `src/vision/caption.ts` — offline Ollama VL caption (+ OCR fallback) → `[IMAGE CAPTION — local]`
- `src/vision/ocr.ts` — local Tesseract + optional Pillow preprocess
- `src/agent/orchestrator.ts` — turn pipeline
- `src/agent/tools.ts` — apply + save
- `src/chat/ChatPanel.ts` — UI
- `src/agent/chatArchive.ts` — saved chats under `.blossom/chats/` (History chip + agent list/search/read tools)
- `hand-off.md` — vision pipeline + open local roadblocks (R1–R6)

Backend rules: `Documents/Blossom/PythonScripts/` — coordinate; do not duplicate disk I/O there.

## When changing the plugin

Prefer verified context injection over hoping the local coder "knows." Language-agnostic path fences + disk checks; HTML href/orphan helpers are OK as specialized cases. After changes: `npm run compile`, reload, test create+edit, link-check with existing siblings, unused delete candidate, auto-apply saves.
